<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jamshedpur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jamshedpur is an industrial city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jharkhand">Jharkhand</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founded as a company town by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tata-steel">Tata Iron and Steel Company</a>. Named after Jamsetji Tata, who planned India's first large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> works, it grew around the plant at Sakchi, which began production in 1912 using iron ore from Mayurbhanj. It remains a major centre of the steel and engineering industries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamshedpur.jpg" alt="Jamshedpur" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shahbaz26 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_City_Jamshedpur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
